{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,75p;790,1022p;1210,1325p;1400,1605p;2205,2270p;2300,2505p;2960,3200p' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,75p;790,1022p;1210,1325p;1400,1605p;2205,2270p;2300,2505p;2960,3200p' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.clojure\n  \"Yang Clojure compiler - Compiles Clojure code into Yin VM Universal AST.\n\n  This is the Clojure-specific compiler in the Yang compiler collection.\n  It transforms Clojure s-expressions into the Universal AST format that\n  the Yin VM can execute. It handles:\n  - Literals (numbers, strings, booleans, nil, collections)\n  - Variables (symbols)\n  - Lambda expressions (fn)\n  - Function application (including stream operations via module system)\n  - Conditionals (if)\n  - Let bindings (let)\n  - Top-level definitions via explicit yin/def store effects\n  - Macro definitions (defmacro)\n\n  Macro support (docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md §10.2):\n  - defmacro is a special form that lowers to ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...))\n    syntax. The lambda node carries `:macro? true`, a frontend-internal fact\n    the encoder (`yin.vm.encoder/program-batch`) turns into a declaration row;\n    the canonical lambda row has no macro slot.\n  - A macro call is an ordinary application. The frontend does no macro\n    lookup: the row-native expander recognizes the call.\n  - compile-program threads a compile-time macro-env naming the defmacros\n    seen so far, only so the native defn lowering yields to a user defn macro.\n\n  Stream operations (stream/make, stream/put, stream/take, >!, <!) are compiled\n  as regular function applications and resolved through the module system at runtime.\n\n  The compiler is written in .cljc format to run on both JVM and Node.js.\"\n  (:refer-clojure :exclude [compile])\n  (:require #?@(:jolt []\n                :cljd []\n                :clj [[clojure.tools.reader :as treader]\n                      [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt]]\n                :cljs [[cljs.tools.reader :as treader]\n                       [cljs.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt]])\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]\n            [yang.tails :as tails]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n\n;; Forward declaration for mutual recursion\n(declare compile-form compile-lambda)\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Call-site occurrence contract C1 (Addendum A, design §2)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; Every final `:application` occurrence of a produced tree carries the\n;; reserved frontend-metadata key `:yang/call-site` with version value `1`\n;; as a plain node key. Projection (`yin.vm/ast-side-tables`) drops the key\n;; from canonical rows and emits it into the frontend-metadata side table\n;; as `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`, where the first\n;; three coordinates are the site id. The key carries no callee identity,\n;; source arity, or ambient classification. It is distinct from\n;; `:yang/site`, the safepoint mark, which travels as node metadata.\n;; Dedicated node kinds (`:dao.stream.apply/call`, stream and\n;; continuation nodes) are not `:application` nodes and are never marked.\n\n(def call-site-key\n  \"The reserved frontend-metadata key of contract C1.\"\n  :yang/call-site)\n\n\n(def call-site-version\n  \"The version value a C1 marker carries.\"\n  1)\n\n\n(def ^:private ^:dynamic *call-site-finalizing*\n  \"True while an owning production entry point compiles a tree, so the\n   recursive `compile-form` calls inside it defer marking to that entry\n  Clojure: (fn [x y] (+ x y))\n  AST: {:type :lambda\n        :params [x y]\n        :body <compiled-body>}\"\n  ([params body env tail?] (compile-lambda params body env tail? initial-macro-env))\n  ([params body env tail? macro-env]\n   (let [new-macro-env (shadow-macro-env macro-env params)\n         ;; a source fn boundary resets the recur target\n         compiled-body (compile-form body true\n                                     (with-locals (dissoc env ::target) params)\n                                     new-macro-env)]\n     (cond-> {:type :lambda, :params (vec params), :body compiled-body}\n       tail? (assoc :tail? true)))))\n\n\n(defn- compile-fn\n  \"Compile (fn [params] body*) where params may hold sequential patterns:\n   each pattern parameter becomes a fresh simple binder, and the body is\n   wrapped in a let that destructures it.\"\n  [params body-forms env tail? macro-env]\n  (let [{simple :params, bindings :bindings} (lower-fn-params params)]\n    (if (some mentions-recur? body-forms)\n      ;; function-level recur: the body runs as a loop over the parameters,\n      ;; so a pattern parameter re-destructures on every iteration\n      (compile-lambda simple\n                      (with-meta (list* 'loop (vec (interleave params simple)) body-forms)\n                        {::fn-loop true})\n                      env tail? macro-env)\n      (let [body (body-expression body-forms)]\n        (compile-lambda simple\n                        (if (seq bindings) (list 'let bindings body) body)\n                        env tail? macro-env)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Argument-vector convention (slice 3b)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; A Yin closure nil-fills missing arguments and drops extras, so a guest\n;; closure cannot observe its call's argument count. Opted in at\n;; `compile-program` (`:convention :arg-vector`), every user fn and defn\n;; instead becomes ONE closure taking ONE vector, branching on its count:\n;;\n;;   (fn ([a] e1) ([a b] e2))\n;;   =>  (fn [dsg__av]\n;;         (if (data/content= (data/count dsg__av) 1)\n;;           (let [a (data/nth dsg__av 0)] e1)\n;;           (if (data/content= (data/count dsg__av) 2)\n;;             (let [a (data/nth dsg__av 0) b (data/nth dsg__av 1)] e2)\n;;             (data/count))))                     ; refused: no such arity\n;;\n;; The dispatch names are module-qualified, which no let binder can shadow.\n;; A call is (f (conj [] a b)) in tail position when the operator is not\n;; statically native; a native name (a primitive or module export, not bound\n;; locally and not defined by the program) is called directly, and in value\n;; position becomes a fresh adapter closure over the same convention. The\n;; program's own macro names stay ordinary applications: the expander\n;; recognizes those calls, so their operands must stay ordinary.\n\n(def ^:private av-sym (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"av\")))\n\n\n(def ^:private default-adapter-arity\n  \"The largest count an adapter admits for a native name with no declared\n   profile (`:native` given as a plain set).\"\n  4)\n\n\n(def ^:private adapter-variadic-cap\n  \"How far an adapter extends a `:variadic` profile arity: an adapter is a\n   finite dispatch, so an open-ended arity needs a stated bound.\"\n  8)\n\n\n(defn- native-name?\n  \"True when `sym` statically names a primitive or host-module export.\"\n  [env sym]\n  (when-let [conv (::convention env)]\n    (and (symbol? sym)\n         (not (contains? (locals env) sym))\n         (not (contains? (::defined env) sym))\n         (or (some? (namespace sym))\n             (contains? (:native conv) sym)))))\n\n\n(defn- macro-call?\n  [env macro-env sym]\n  (and (symbol? sym)\n       (not (contains? (locals env) sym))\n       (or (contains? macro-env sym)\n           (contains? (:macros (::convention env)) sym))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The continuation lane (slice 5, ported off the outcome model)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; Opted in with `:outcomes true` beside the argument-vector convention (the\n;; flag now selects the continuation lane, not the retired outcome tuples).\n;; Guest functions return plain values; `throw` lowers to `clj/throw`, `try`\n;; to `clj/try`/`clj/try-finally` (the `%capture` handler-stack family), and a\n;; guest call delivers an escaping condition through the §8.10.7 raise exit.\n;; The public entry installs the same bridge before argument binding. Only the\n;; `compile-program` boundary still wraps the program in `[:yin.k/ok value]` /\n;; `[:yin.k/error raised]` for the harness. `ex-info` becomes a portable map\n;; under namespaced keys, `ex-message`/`ex-data` its accessors. Generated names\n;; carry the reserved `dsg__` prefix; the program pre-pass keeps user code out\n;; of that prefix. A macro call is opaque to the pass: the expander owns it.\n\n(def ^:private ok-tag :yin.k/ok)\n\n(def ^:private error-tag :yin.k/error)\n\n\n(defn- outcomes?\n  [env]\n  (some? (::outcomes env)))\n\n\n(defn- rebuild\n  \"A list of `items` carrying the reader metadata of `form`.\"\n  [form items]\n  (let [out (apply list items)]\n    (if-let [m (meta form)]\n      (with-meta out m)\n      out)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The clj continuation family (R3 §8.10.7; the (B) port)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; The port converges clojure's exception lowering onto the continuation\n;; encoding: a `%capture` handler stack in a dynamic-context cell, exactly\n;; like the py/ts/php preludes (`yang.clojure.prelude` carries the reference\n;; implementation under `clj/`). A source `(throw e)` lowers to `clj/throw`,\n;; `(try ...)` to `clj/try`/`clj/try-finally`, and function bodies return\n;; plain values. A guest call delivers a callee's escaping condition through\n;; the §8.10.7 raise exit, and the public entry installs the same bridge.\n;; Ordinary thrown values remain raw; protocol conditions travel in a\n;; provenance carrier. `compile-program` emits this family\n;; inline (the linked runtime binds the same family from the prelude); it\n;; routes the capture-sensitive primitives through the `dsg__*` helpers so a\n;; program definition of `get`/`assoc`/`=` cannot capture a frame access.\n\n(def ^:private continuation-family\n  \"The `clj/` continuation family, `[key form]` in prelude notation (each\n   form is read with `u/sexp->uast`). Mirrors `yang.clojure.prelude`'s\n   escapes section, minus `call-ec`/`unwind-to` (clojure has no\n   break/continue/return escapes). The handler stack is a chain of frames\n   [tag payload rest n]; a `:handler` frame holds the continuation\n   `clj/raise` delivers to, a `:finally` frame a one-argument thunk every\n   exit through it runs.\"\n  '[[clj/ctx (fn [hs] (dsg__assoc {} :handlers hs))]\n    [clj/handlers (fn [] (dsg__get (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers))]\n    [clj/set-handlers!\n     (fn [hs]\n       (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx (dsg__assoc (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers hs)))]\n    [clj/restore! (fn [saved] (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx saved))]\n    [clj/frame-depth (fn [hs] (if (dsg__equal hs nil) 0 (dsg__get hs 3)))]\n    [clj/frame\n     (fn [tag payload rest]\n       (conj (conj (conj (conj [] tag) payload) rest)\n             (+ 1 (clj/frame-depth rest))))]\n    [clj/pop-frame\n     (fn [hs]\n       (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx\n                  (dsg__assoc (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers (dsg__get hs 2))))]\n    [clj/raise\n     (fn [e]\n       (let [hs (clj/handlers)]\n         (if (dsg__equal hs nil)\n           (dsg__get e :clj/no-handler)\n           (if (dsg__equal (dsg__get hs 0) :finally)\n             (do (clj/pop-frame hs) ((dsg__get hs 1) e) (clj/raise e))\n             ((dsg__get hs 1) e)))))]\n    [clj/throw (fn [e] (clj/raise e))]\n    [clj/try\n     (fn [body handler]\n       (let [saved (cell/get clj.rt/ctx)\n             flag (cell/new :first)]\n         ((fn [r]\n            (if (dsg__equal (cell/get flag) :first)\n              (do (cell/set! flag :re-entered)\n                  (clj/set-handlers! (clj/frame :handler r (dsg__get saved :handlers)))\n                  (let [v (body)] (do (clj/restore! saved) v)))\n              (do (clj/restore! saved) (handler r))))\n          (%capture))))]\n    [clj/try-finally\n     (fn [body fin]\n       (let [saved (cell/get clj.rt/ctx)]\n         (do (clj/set-handlers! (clj/frame :finally fin (dsg__get saved :handlers)))\n             (let [v (body)]\n               (do (clj/restore! saved) (fin nil) v)))))]])\n\n\n(def ^:private ex-message-form\n  '(fn [dsg__value] (dsg__get dsg__value :yin.k/message)))\n\n\n(def ^:private ex-data-form\n  '(fn [dsg__value] (dsg__get dsg__value :yin.k/data)))\n\n\n(def ^:private continuation-uast\n  \"The continuation family tree: define every `clj/` entry (store-defined,\n   like `yang.core.call/uast`) then allocate the `clj.rt/ctx` cell. The\n   family's capture-sensitive primitives are the `dsg__*` names, bound at\n   emission by `compile-program`.\"\n  (u/then\n    (reduce (fn [ast [key form]]\n              (u/then ast (u/def! key (u/sexp->uast form))))\n            (u/lit nil)\n            continuation-family)\n    (u/def! 'clj.rt/ctx\n            (u/app (u/v 'cell/new) (u/app (u/v 'clj/ctx) (u/lit nil))))))\n\n\n(def continuation-family-names\n  \"The `clj/` continuation-family store definitions `compile-program` emits\n   inline (plus the `clj.rt/ctx` cell): compiler-bound names an admission scan\n   must accept, like the preamble's `dsg__*` helpers. Exposed so a harness\n   admission check stays in sync with the family instead of hardcoding it.\"\n  (into #{'clj.rt/ctx} (map first continuation-family)))\n\n\n(defn- rewrite-ex-info\n  \"(ex-info msg data cause?) as the portable map holding its parts. The\n   accessors read through the generated exception wrapper: a retained\n   condition's wrapper carries the original payload privately, so\n   (ex-message e)/(ex-data e) answer the payload's parts while a plain\n   value still answers by keyword lookup.\"\n  [form]\n    (check-binder! p params)))\n\n\n(defn- outcome-node\n  [tag value]\n  (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/lit []) (u/lit tag)) value))\n\n\n(defn- call-entry\n  \"The unary public entry, closed over a private argument-vector body. It\n   installs the exception bridge (`clj/try`) before argument binding, so an\n   escaping raise forwards an authenticated condition or wraps an ordinary\n   value as `:yang.call/thrown` exactly once after cleanup.\"\n  []\n  (let [body (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"body\"))\n        invocation (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"invocation\"))\n        positional (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/positional))\n        named (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/named))\n        raise (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/raise))\n        binding-error (u/app\n                        (u/v 'clj/throw)\n                        (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n                               (u/lit :yin.k/message)\n                               (u/lit \"Clojure functions do not accept named arguments\")\n                               (u/lit :yin.k/data)\n                               (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n                                      (u/lit :yang.call/named) named)))\n        forged-refusal (u/app\n                         (u/v 'clj/throw)\n                         (u/lit {:yin.k/message\n                                 \"Invocation is neither an authenticated packet nor an invocation record\"\n                                 :yin.k/data {}}))\n        ;; The record path: bind and run the body under clj/try, delivering\n        ;; an authenticated condition or a fresh :yang.call/thrown condition.\n        entry-body (u/app\n                     (u/v 'clj/try)\n                     (u/lam [] (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__empty) named)\n                                          (u/app (u/v body) positional)\n                                          binding-error))\n                     (u/lam ['dsg__e]\n                            (u/let1 'dsg__provenance\n                                    (u/app (u/v 'cell/dsg__provenance) (u/v 'dsg__e))\n                                    (assoc (u/app raise\n                                                  (u/if-node\n                                                    (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal) (u/v 'dsg__provenance) (u/lit nil))\n                                                    (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/thrown) (u/v 'dsg__e))\n                                                    (u/v 'dsg__provenance))) :tail? true))))\n        ;; The private lane forwards the body's plain value in tail position\n        ;; (a raise from it propagates to the caller's own handler — the lane\n        ;; installs no bridge). The compiler's token packet, a two-element\n        ;; vector [token args], selects it on the SAME unary entry. A guest\n        ;; cannot forge the token; maps keep the ordinary record path.\n        packet (u/if-node\n                 (u/app (u/v 'data/vector?) (u/v invocation))\n                 (u/if-node\n                   (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n                          (u/app (u/v 'data/count) (u/v invocation))\n                          (u/lit 2))\n                   (u/if-node\n                     (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n                            (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v invocation) (u/lit 0))\n                            (u/v 'dsg__call_token))\n                     (u/app (u/v body) (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v invocation) (u/lit 1)))\n                     forged-refusal)\n                   forged-refusal)\n                 entry-body)\n        entry (u/lam [invocation] packet)]\n    (u/lam [body] entry)))\n\n\n(defn- admit-call-descriptor\n  \"Admit a descriptor constructed by trusted UAST/profile code. This is not\n   a source form: entry-spelled source maps never pass through this constructor.\"\n  [descriptor-ast tail?]\n  (let [descriptor-name 'dsg__descriptor\n        canonical (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) descriptor-ast\n                         (u/lit :clj/admission) (u/lit nil))\n        ;; The factory closure captures the canonical descriptor and private\n        ;; token. Projection reconstructs and compares that opaque closure;\n        ;; it never applies a source-supplied predicate. An equal immutable\n        ;; reconstruction is the same value, not admission of different data.\n        witness (u/app (u/v 'dsg__make_admission) (u/v descriptor-name))\n        published (u/let1 descriptor-name canonical\n                          (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/v descriptor-name)\n                                 (u/lit :clj/admission) witness))]\n    (cond-> (u/mark-tails published)\n      tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n\n\n(defn- compile-call-descriptor\n  \"Publish a private body through a canonical constructor-created entry.\"\n  [body-ast tail?]\n  (admit-call-descriptor\n    (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n           (u/lit :yang.call/entry) (u/app (u/v 'dsg__make_entry) body-ast)\n           (u/lit :clj/type) (u/lit :function))\n    tail?))\n\n\n(defn- compile-av-fn\n  \"Compile arities [{:params :body}] to one closure over an argument vector.\n   `fn-name` names the function in an arity error outcome. Under the outcome\n   model the published value is an immutable common-call descriptor.\"\n  ([arities env tail? macro-env] (compile-av-fn arities env tail? macro-env nil nil))\n  ([arities env tail? macro-env fn-name] (compile-av-fn arities env tail? macro-env fn-name nil))\n  ([arities env tail? macro-env fn-name source]\n   (let [arities (mapv (fn [{:keys [params body]}]\n                         (check-av-params! params)\n                         {:n (count params)\n                          :form (av-let env macro-env params body)})\n                       arities)\n         body (compile-lambda [av-sym] (av-dispatch env fn-name source arities)\n                              env false macro-env)]\n     (if (outcomes? env)\n       (compile-call-descriptor body tail?)\n       (cond-> body tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))\n   issuer never certified. A map that fails this pre-filter is never\n   asked and never dereferenced: it routes to ordinary map\n   invocation, which grants no cell capability.\"\n  [callee]\n  (let [seal (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) callee (u/lit :seal))]\n    (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n                      (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) callee (u/lit :type))\n                      (u/lit :cell-ref))\n               (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/contains?) callee (u/lit :id))\n                          (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/contains?) callee (u/lit :seal))\n                                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n                                                       (u/app (u/v 'data/count) callee)\n                                                       (u/lit 3))\n                                                (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/string?) seal)\n                                                           (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n                                                                             (u/app (u/v 'data/str-length) seal)\n                                                                             (u/lit 64))\n                                                                      (u/lit true)\n                                                                      (u/lit false))\n                                                           (u/lit false))\n                                                (u/lit false))\n                                     (u/lit false))\n                          (u/lit false))\n               (u/lit false))))\n\n\n(defn- compile-guest-call\n  \"Admit a source operator before common invocation. The raise exit delivers\n   the callee's escaping condition into the clj continuation: a\n   `:yang.call/thrown` condition delivers its payload (the caught value IS the\n   payload), while a protocol condition is retained in a provenance carrier.\n   Only generated UAST implementation calls apply private closures directly.\"\n  [callee-ast arguments-ast env tail?]\n  (if-not (outcomes? env)\n    (cond-> (u/app callee-ast arguments-ast)\n      tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n    (let [callee (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"callee\"))\n          arguments (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"arguments\"))\n          condition (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"condition\"))\n          raise-exit (u/lam [condition]\n                            (assoc (u/app (u/v 'clj/raise)\n                                          (u/if-node\n                                            (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n                                                   (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v condition)\n                                                          (u/lit :yang.call/reason))\n                                                   (u/lit :yang.call/thrown))\n                                            (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v condition)\n                                                   (u/lit :yang.call/value))\n                                            (u/app (u/v 'cell/dsg__new-provenance)\n                                                   (u/v condition) (u/v condition))))\n                                   :tail? true))\n          common-call (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/invoke) (u/v callee) (u/v arguments)\n                             (u/lit []) raise-exit)\n          refused (u/let1 condition\n                          (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/condition)\n                                 (u/lit :yang.call/not-callable)\n                                 (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n                                        (u/lit :yang.call/callee) (u/v callee)))\n                          (assoc (u/app (u/v 'clj/raise)\n                                        (u/app (u/v 'cell/dsg__new-provenance)\n                                               (u/v condition) (u/v condition))) :tail? true))\n          admitted (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__admitted?) (u/v callee))\n                              common-call refused)\n          ;; A callee carrying a call entry is convention territory whether it\n          ;; admits or forges one, so admission rules it. Everything else is a\n          ;; data-side invocation - a collection lookup or a raw closure call -\n          ;; owned by the guest library's invoker, reached the same way.\n          value-call (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/invoke)\n                            (u/v 'invoke-value)\n                            (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/lit []) (u/v callee) (u/v arguments))\n                            (u/lit [])\n                            raise-exit)\n          routed (if (::invoker env)\n                   (u/if-node\n                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/map?) (u/v callee))\n                                (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/contains?) (u/v callee) (u/lit :yang.call/entry))\n                                           (u/lit true)\n                                           ;; the shape is only WHEN to ask (ruling of\n                                           ;; record, rule 2): the heap answers\n                                           ;; `cell/authentic?`, and an unauthenticated\n                                           ;; shape takes ordinary map invocation\n                                           (u/if-node (cell-ref-shaped-node (u/v callee))\n                                                      (u/app (u/v 'cell/authentic?) (u/v callee))\n                                                      (u/lit false)))\n                                (u/lit false))\n                     admitted\n                     value-call)\n                   admitted)]\n      (cond-> (u/mark-tails (u/let1 callee callee-ast\n                                    (u/let1 arguments arguments-ast routed)))\n        tail? (assoc :tail? true)))))\n\n\n(defn- compile-apply\n  \"(apply f a b coll) as one application of f to the assembled argument\n   vector (into [a b] (vec coll)): the convention's own calling shape, so it\n   serves a guest closure and an adapted native alike.\"\n  [operands env tail? macro-env]\n  (when (< (count operands) 2)\n    (reject! \"apply takes a function and an argument collection\"\n             {:operands (count operands)}))\n  (let [[f & more] operands\n        lead (vec (butlast more))\n        coll-form (list 'vec (last more))]\n    (compile-guest-call (compile-form f false env macro-env)\n                        (compile-form (if (seq lead)\n                                        (list 'data/into lead coll-form)\n                                        coll-form)\n                                      false env macro-env)\n                        env tail?)))\n\n\n(defn- compile-av-application\n  [operator operands env tail? macro-env]\n  (cond\n    (apply-call? env operator) (compile-apply operands env tail? macro-env)\n\n    ;; (:k m) / (:k m default): a static lookup\n    (keyword? operator)\n    (do (when-not (<= 1 (count operands) 2)\n          (reject! \"A keyword call takes a map and an optional default\"\n                   {:keyword operator, :operands (count operands)}))\n        (when (contains? (locals env) 'get)\n          (reject! \"A local binding of get would capture a keyword lookup\"\n                   {:keyword operator}))\n        (cond-> {:type :application\n                 :operator {:type :variable, :name 'get}\n                 :operands (into [(if (outcomes? env)\n                                    (u/app (u/v 'dsg__condition_view)\n                                           (compile-form (first operands) false env macro-env))\n                                    (compile-form (first operands) false env macro-env))\n                                  (compile-literal operator false)]\n                                 (map #(compile-form % false env macro-env))\n                                 (rest operands))}\n          tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n\n    (and (outcomes? env) (= operator 'yang.call/eligible?))\n    (let [candidate 'dsg__eligibility_candidate]\n      (cond-> (u/mark-tails\n                (apply u/app\n                       (u/lam [candidate]\n                              (u/if-node\n                                (u/app (u/v 'dsg__admitted?) (u/v candidate))\n                                (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/eligible?) (u/v candidate))\n                                (u/lit false)))\n                       (map #(compile-form % false env macro-env) operands)))\n        tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n\n    (and (outcomes? env)\n         (#{'yang.call/invoke 'yang.call/invoke-with} operator)\n         (<= 4 (count operands)))\n    (let [bindings (into ['dsg__invocation_candidate]\n                         (map #(symbol (str \"dsg__invocation_operand_\" %)))\n                         (range (dec (count operands))))\n          compile-operand #(compile-form % false env macro-env)]\n      (cond-> (u/mark-tails\n                (apply u/app\n                       (u/lam bindings\n                              (u/if-node\n                                (u/app (u/v 'dsg__admitted?) (u/v (first bindings)))\n                                (apply u/app (u/v operator) (map u/v bindings))\n                                (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/transfer)\n                                       (u/v (nth bindings 3))\n                                       (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/condition)\n                                              (u/lit :yang.call/not-callable)\n                                              (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n                                                     (u/lit :yang.call/callee)\n                                                     (u/v (first bindings)))))))\n                       (map compile-operand operands)))\n        tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n\n    ;; a statically intra-unit defn/defn- under the outcome model: apply the\n    ;; unit's public entry with the compiler's token packet (a two-element\n    ;; vector: [token args]) - the private lane on the same unary entry,\n    ;; one conj and one lookup, no record construction\n    (intra-unit-fn? env operator)\n    (cond-> {:type :application\n             :operator {:type :variable, :name 'dsg__intra_call}\n             :operands [(cond-> {:type :variable, :name operator}\n                          (seq (meta operator)) (with-meta (meta operator)))\n                        (compile-form (vec operands) false env macro-env)]}\n      tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n\n    ;; A native lookup projects a carrier only for observation. The original\n    ;; reference remains available for saving or rethrowing.\n    (native-name? env operator)\n    (cond-> {:type :application\n             :operator (cond-> {:type :variable, :name operator}\n                         (seq (meta operator)) (with-meta (meta operator)))\n             :operands (mapv (fn [i operand]\n                               (let [ast (compile-form operand false env macro-env)]\n                                 (if (and (outcomes? env) (= operator 'get) (zero? i))\n                                   (u/app (u/v 'dsg__condition_view) ast)\n                                   ast))) (range) operands)}\n      tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n\n    ;; a compiler-internal helper introduced by the pre-pass (the exception\n    ;; accessors): a direct application, never a guest invocation\n    (and (symbol? operator) (reserved-name? operator))\n    (cond-> {:type :application\n             :operator (cond-> {:type :variable, :name operator}\n                         (seq (meta operator)) (with-meta (meta operator)))\n             :operands (mapv #(compile-form % false env macro-env) operands)}\n      tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n\n    ;; anything else: one guest invocation, in tail position when the call is\n                   ::defined-fns defined-fns\n                   ::invoker (boolean (some #(and (seq? %) (= 'defn (first %))\n                                                  (= 'invoke-value (second %))\n                                                  (:yin.k/invoker (meta (second %)))) forms))}\n            (:outcomes opts) (assoc ::outcomes {:adapters (or (:adapters opts) {})}))))))\n\n\n(defn- check-program-symbols!\n  \"The program pre-pass. Quoted data is exempt. The reserved prefix names\n   compiler temporaries, so no user symbol may carry it in ANY position\n   (binder, reference, definition name); `loop` and `recur` are special forms,\n   so they may only head a list, never stand as a value or a binder.\"\n  [form]\n  (cond\n    (symbol? form)\n    (do (when (reserved-name? form)\n          (reject! \"Symbol uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n                   {:symbol form, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n        (when (and (nil? (namespace form)) (contains? #{'loop 'recur} form))\n          (reject! (str form \" is only legal in operator position\") {:symbol form})))\n    (seq? form)\n    (when-not (= 'quote (first form))\n      (let [head (first form)]\n        (when (and (symbol? head) (reserved-name? head))\n          (reject! \"Symbol uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n                   {:symbol head, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n        (when-not (symbol? head)\n          (check-program-symbols! head))\n        (run! check-program-symbols! (rest form))))\n    (map? form) (run! check-program-symbols! (concat (keys form) (vals form)))\n    (coll? form) (run! check-program-symbols! form)))\n\n\n(defn- lower-top-form\n  \"A non-definition top-level expression lowers like a function body (plain\n   values, `throw`/`try` onto the continuation family); definitions keep\n   their own lowering.\"\n  [env macro-env form]\n  (if (and (seq? form) (contains? #{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} (first form)))\n    form\n    (lower-function-body env macro-env [] [form])))\n\n\n(defn- top-boundary\n  \"The top-level exception boundary: run `ast` under `clj/try`, answering\n   `[:yin.k/ok value]` on normal return and `[:yin.k/error raised]` on a\n   raise. The `[:yin.k/ok|error]` wrapper is the harness contract (a linked\n   entry's `clj/unwrap-outcome` removes one level); inside it, function\n   bodies return plain values and a raise is the only error channel.\"\n  [ast]\n  (u/app (u/v 'clj/try)\n         (u/lam [] (outcome-node ok-tag ast))\n         (u/lam ['dsg__e]\n                (u/let1 'dsg__p (u/app (u/v 'cell/dsg__provenance) (u/v 'dsg__e))\n                        (outcome-node error-tag\n                                      (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal) (u/v 'dsg__p) (u/lit nil))\n                                                 (u/v 'dsg__e) (u/v 'dsg__p)))))))\n\n\n(defn compile-program\n  \"Compile a sequence of Clojure forms into a single Universal AST.\n   Top-level defs compile to explicit yin/def store writes, sequenced via lambda.\n   Top-level defmacros are lowered to ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...)) syntax\n   with :macro? true on the lambda; the encoder turns that flag into a\n   declaration row and the expander, not this compiler, recognizes calls.\n   The three-argument form takes `opts` opting into the argument-vector\n                                                     (assoc macro-env\n                                                            (strip-symbol-meta (second head))\n                                                            {:type :user}))}\n                                :operands [(discard-result defined)]}\n                         tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n                     ;; def: sequence with current macro-env\n                     (and (seq? head) (= 'def (first head)))\n                     (let [[_ name value] head\n                           value (if (outcomes? env)\n                                   (lower-function-body env macro-env [] [value])\n                                   value)]\n                       (cond-> {:type     :application\n                                :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['_]\n                                           :body (go rest-forms macro-env)}\n                                :operands [(discard-result (compile-def name value env false macro-env))]}\n                         tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n                     ;; single form\n                     (= 1 (count forms))\n                     (compile-form head tail? (assoc env ::top-level true) macro-env)\n                     ;; sequence\n                     :else\n                     (cond-> {:type     :application\n                              :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['_]\n                                         :body (go rest-forms macro-env)}\n                              :operands [(discard-result\n                                           (compile-form head false\n                                                         (assoc env ::top-level true) macro-env))]}\n                       tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))]\n       (annotate-call-sites\n         (cond->> (go forms initial-macro-env)\n           (outcomes? env) top-boundary\n           (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__condition_view\n                                   (u/sexp->uast\n                                     '(fn [dsg__value]\n                                        (if (dsg__equal (cell/dsg__provenance dsg__value) nil)\n                                          dsg__value\n                                          (cell/get dsg__value)))))\n           ;; The two sibling closures share one frame: separate bindings would\n           ;; retain one extra helper environment in every closure a guest\n           ;; captures (the machine-data validation bound notices).\n           (outcomes? env) (#(u/app\n                               (u/lam '[dsg__admitted? dsg__intra_call] %)\n                               (u/sexp->uast\n                                 '(fn [dsg__candidate]\n                                    (if (data/map? dsg__candidate)\n                                      ;; A map is offered to the dereference\n                                      ;; only when the heap authenticates it\n                                      ;; (ruling of record, rule 2), as the\n                                      ;; descriptor projection treats a\n                                      ;; cell-backed callable\n                                      ;; (yang.antlr.md 8.10.2), whose entry\n                                      ;; lives in the cell contents. The\n                                      ;; issued format (`:type :cell-ref`,\n                                      ;; `:id`, `:seal`, no other entries, a\n                                      ;; 64-character string seal) is only\n                                      ;; the pre-filter for WHEN to ask;\n                                      ;; `cell/authentic?` — the issuer's\n                                      ;; own heap+seal answer — decides, so\n                                      ;; any `:id` spelling may be asked\n                                      ;; about and the r4 heap-id-language\n                                      ;; discriminator is retired. A shape\n                                      ;; the heap does not authenticate is\n                                      ;; data: it falls to the witness\n                                      ;; branch and, entryless, is no more\n                                      ;; admitted than any other source map,\n                                      ;; so its invocation stays ordinary\n                                      ;; map data. An authenticated\n                                      ;; reference dereferences; an\n                                      ;; authenticated cell whose contents\n                                      ;; carry no callable entry is not\n                                      ;; admitted (authentication is not\n                                      ;; authorization, rule 3), and the\n                                      ;; call-site routing that consulted\n                                      ;; here refuses it as not-callable.\n                                      (let [dsg__cell-ref?\n                                            (if (dsg__equal\n                                                  (dsg__get dsg__candidate :type)\n                                                  :cell-ref)\n                                              (if (data/contains? dsg__candidate\n                                                                  :id)\n                                                (if (data/contains? dsg__candidate\n                                                                    :seal)\n                                                  (if (dsg__equal\n                                                        (data/count dsg__candidate)\n                                                        3)\n                                                    (if (data/string?\n                                                          (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n                                                                    :seal))\n                                                      (if (dsg__equal\n                                                            (data/str-length\n                                                              (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n                                                                        :seal))\n                                                            64)\n                                                        true\n                                                        false)\n                                                      false)\n                                                    false)\n                                                  false)\n                                                false)\n                                              false)]\n                                        (if dsg__cell-ref?\n                                          (if (cell/authentic? dsg__candidate)\n                                            (let [dsg__descriptor\n                                                  (cell/get dsg__candidate)\n                                                  dsg__entry\n                                                  (dsg__get dsg__descriptor\n                                                            :yang.call/entry)]\n                                              (data/callable? dsg__entry))\n                                            false)\n                                          (let [dsg__entry\n                                                (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n                                                          :yang.call/entry)\n                                                dsg__witness\n                                                (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n                                                          :clj/admission)]\n                                            (if (data/callable? dsg__entry)\n                                              (if (data/callable? dsg__witness)\n                                                (dsg__equal\n                                                  dsg__witness\n                                                  (dsg__make_admission\n                                                    (dsg__assoc dsg__candidate\n                                                                :clj/admission\n                                                                nil)))\n                                                false)\n                                              false))))\n                                      false)))\n                               ;; The intra-unit dispatcher: resolve the unit's public entry,\n                               ;; apply it with the compiler's token packet [token args] - one\n                               ;; variadic conj and one application, no record construction.\n                               ;; Non-map callees refuse.\n                               (u/sexp->uast\n                                 (list 'fn '[dsg__callee dsg__args]\n                                       (list 'if '(data/map? dsg__callee)\n                                             (list (list (if (contains? (::defined env) 'get)\n                                                           'dsg__get\n                                                           'get)\n                                                         'dsg__callee\n                                                         :yang.call/entry)\n                                                   (list 'conj '[]\n                                                         'dsg__call_token\n                                                         'dsg__args))\n                                             '(let [dsg__condition (yang.call/condition\n                                                                     :yang.call/not-callable\n                                                                     (dsg__assoc {} :yang.call/callee dsg__callee))]\n                                                (clj/raise (cell/dsg__new-provenance dsg__condition dsg__condition))))))))\n           (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__make_entry (call-entry))\n           (outcomes? env) (u/let1\n                             'dsg__make_admission\n                             (u/sexp->uast\n                               '(fn [dsg__descriptor]\n                                  (fn [dsg__candidate]\n                                    (if (data/callable? dsg__call_token)\n                                      (dsg__get dsg__descriptor :yang.call/entry)\n                                      nil)))))\n           ;; The exception accessors and the continuation family. The\n           ;; `dsg__ex_message`/`dsg__ex_data` accessors read the portable\n           ;; ex-info map; the continuation family (`clj/try`, `clj/throw`,\n           ;; `clj/raise`, ...) is the port's `%capture` handler-stack scheme,\n           ;; emitted inline (the linked runtime binds the same family from the\n           ;; prelude). Its capture-sensitive primitives are the `dsg__*`\n           ;; names bound outside it.\n           (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__ex_message\n                                   (u/sexp->uast ex-message-form))\n           (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__ex_data\n                                   (u/sexp->uast ex-data-form))\n           ;; A linked unit shares the required clj module's handler stack.\n           ;; Its inline counterpart names the private clj.rt/ctx store key,\n           ;; which cannot be read from a different module.\n           (and (outcomes? env) (not (:linked-runtime opts))) (u/then\n                                                                (discard-result continuation-uast))\n           (outcomes? env) (u/then\n                             (discard-result\n                               (u/app (u/lam '[get = assoc empty?] call/uast)\n                                      (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n                                      (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/v 'dsg__empty))))\n           (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__call_token (u/lam [] (u/lit nil)))\n           ;; Guest closures keep captured environments portable: binding host\n           ;; primitive values here would make UCF machine-data validation fail.\n           ;; These helpers cover generated map lookups/writes and comparisons;\n           ;; conj/vec are already protected by the convention's binder checks.\n           ;; Evaluate siblings outside each other's bindings to avoid retaining\n           ;; a chain of redundant helper environments.\n           (outcomes? env) (#(u/app\n                               (u/lam '[dsg__get dsg__equal dsg__assoc dsg__empty] %)\n                               (if (contains? (::defined env) 'get)\n                                 (u/sexp->uast\n                                   '(fn [m k]\n                                      (if (data/map? m)\n                                        (let [find (fn [self entries]\n                                                     (if (data/content= 0 (data/count entries))\n                                                       nil\n                                                       (let [pair (data/nth entries 0)]\n                                                         (if (data/content= k (data/nth pair 0))\n                                                           (data/nth pair 1)\n                                                           (self self (data/subvec entries 1))))))]\n                                          (find find (vec m)))\n                                        nil)))\n                                 (u/sexp->uast '(fn [m k] (get m k))))\n                               (u/sexp->uast '(fn [a b] (data/content= a b)))\n                               (if (contains? (::defined env) 'assoc)\n                                 (u/sexp->uast\n                                   '(fn [m k v k2 v2 k3 v3]\n                                      (let [one (conj m (conj [] k v))]\n                                        (if (data/content= k2 nil)\n                                          one\n                                          (let [two (conj one (conj [] k2 v2))]\n                  (recur (concat (rest todo) (mentions (by-name n))) (conj seen n))) seen))]\n      (let [source (concat forms (map by-name needed))\n            needed (if (some dynamic-call? source) (close ['invoke-value] needed) needed)]\n        (filterv #(contains? needed (second %)) library)))))\n\n\n(defn compile\n  \"Main compiler entry point.\n\n  Compiles a Clojure form into Yin VM Universal AST.\n\n  Examples:\n    (compile 42)\n    => {:type :literal, :value 42}\n\n    (compile '(+ 1 2))\n    => {:type :application\n        :operator {:type :variable, :name +}\n        :operands [{:type :literal, :value 1}\n                   {:type :literal, :value 2}]}\n\n    (compile '(fn [x] (* x 2)))\n    => {:type :lambda\n        :params [x]\n        :body {:type :application\n               :operator {:type :variable, :name *}\n               :operands [{:type :variable, :name x}\n                          {:type :literal, :value 2}]}}\"\n  [form]\n  ;; the single-form entry runs the same reserved-prefix pre-pass as\n  ;; `compile-program`, so a REPL one-liner can no more spell a\n  ;; compiler-private (`dsg__`) name than a whole program can. Trusted\n  ;; compiler construction never reaches `compile`: it builds its own\n  ;; `dsg__` temporaries via `compile-form` directly.\n  (check-program-symbols! form)\n  (compile-form form true {}))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The linked runtime entry (the conformance matrix round, yang.antlr.md\n;; section 8.10)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; A linked clojure program is published as an ordinary linker module whose\n;; one export, `body`, is its unmodified lowered unit, and run under its own\n;; entry, `clj/run-main` (the `clj` runtime module, yang.clojure.prelude).\n;; `read-forms` is the frontend's parser — the reader itself — and\n;; `lower-unit` lowers what it reads to the entry's argument: one thunk\n;; whose call runs the program compiled under the argument-vector\n;; convention and the outcome model over the guest library, with every\n;; top-level definition published to the runtime global namespace\n;; (`clj/define-global!`/`clj/global-get`), as a Python def lands in\n;; its module's globals. No call node is rewritten and no foreign\n;; `:code` is extracted: the unit is the program's own lowering,\n;; wrapped.\n\n(def unit-opts\n  \"The `compile-program` opts a linked unit compiles with: the\n   argument-vector convention with the outcome model over the guest\n   library's adapters. The required clj module supplies the continuation\n   family; VM primitives are callable directly by bare name.\"\n  {:convention :arg-vector,\n   :outcomes true,\n   :linked-runtime true,\n   :adapters library-adapters,\n   :native vm/primitive-profiles})\n\n\n(def top-defining-operators\n  \"The operators whose second element names a top-level definition.\"\n  '#{def defn defn- defmacro})\n\n\n(defn read-forms\n  \"Every form `source` text reads. The reader is the parser: a malformed\n   source throws, as any frontend's refused parse does.\n\n   Source-string compilation is a JVM/Node capability (tools.reader is\n   an mvn dependency, absent from the jolt host's source-root classpath\n   — the jolt lane loads compiled output and ships source strings to\n   remote evaluators, so this is unreachable there; the honest error\n   says so if ever reached).\"\n  [source]\n  #?(:cljd (throw (ex-info \"Source-string compilation requires the JVM/Node reader; ClojureDart compiles from forms\"\n                           {:yang.clojure/reader :unavailable-on-cljd}))\n     :jolt (throw (ex-info \"Source-string compilation requires the JVM/Node reader; the jolt host compiles from forms or delegates source reading to its remote evaluators\"\n                           {:yang.clojure/reader :unavailable-on-jolt}))\n     :default\n     (let [rd (rt/string-push-back-reader source)]\n       (loop [forms []]\n         (let [form (treader/read rd false ::eof)]\n           (if (= form ::eof)\n             forms\n             (recur (conj forms form))))))))\n\n\n(defn top-level-names\n  \"The names `forms` define at the top level, in order: the second element\n   of each def/defn/defn-/defmacro head.\"\n  [forms]\n  (into []\n        (comp (filter #(and (seq? %) (contains? top-defining-operators (first %))))\n              (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second)))\n        forms))\n\n\n(declare publish-to-globals)\n\n\n(defn- globals-child\n  [x names bound]\n  (cond\n    (and (map? x) (contains? x :type)) (publish-to-globals x names bound)\n    (vector? x) (mapv #(globals-child % names bound) x)\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn- publish-to-globals\n  \"Rewrite the compiled `node` for the linked unit: a top-level\n   definition in `names` becomes a `clj/define-global!` write and a free\n   read of one becomes a `clj/global-get`, both under the name's string.\n   The `names` a unit is lowered with are its own top-level definitions,\n   its guest library's and the projected names the composition bound in\n   the runtime global namespace, so a projected export and a definition\n   read through the one binding: a definition the unit itself runs\n   publishes after the projection and shadows it. A store definition\n   inside the unit thunk is conditional to the linker, so no body read\n   of it discharges (the runtime preludes avoid this by keeping every\n   definition at module level); the runtime global namespace is the\n   linked unit's definition table instead, as a Python module body\n   writes its dictionary. Lexically bound names, quoted literals and\n   macro definitions keep their store shape: a macro is not a runtime\n   value.\"\n  [node names bound]\n  (case (:type node)\n    :literal node\n    :vm/current-continuation node\n    :variable (if (and (contains? names (:name node))\n                       (not (contains? bound (:name node))))\n                (u/app (u/v 'clj/global-get) (u/lit (str (:name node))))\n                node)\n    :lambda (assoc node :body (publish-to-globals (:body node) names\n                                                  (into bound (:params node))))\n    :application\n    (if (and (= 'yin/def (get-in node [:operator :name]))\n             (= 2 (count (:operands node)))\n             (= :literal (:type (first (:operands node))))\n             (contains? names (:value (first (:operands node)))))\n      (u/app (u/v 'clj/define-global!)\n             (u/lit (str (:value (first (:operands node)))))\n             (publish-to-globals (second (:operands node)) names bound))\n      (assoc node\n             :operator (publish-to-globals (:operator node) names bound)\n             :operands (mapv #(publish-to-globals % names bound)\n                             (:operands node))))\n    :if (cond-> node\n          (contains? node :test)\n          (assoc :test (publish-to-globals (:test node) names bound))\n          (contains? node :consequent)\n          (assoc :consequent (publish-to-globals (:consequent node) names bound))\n          (contains? node :alternate)\n          (assoc :alternate (publish-to-globals (:alternate node) names bound)))\n    (reduce (fn [n k]\n              (let [v (get n k)]\n                (if (or (and (map? v) (contains? v :type)) (vector? v))\n                  (assoc n k (globals-child v names bound))\n                  n)))\n            node (keys node))))\n\n\n(defn lower-unit\n  \"The `clj/run-main` entry's unit for the top-level source `forms`: one\n   thunk whose call runs the program — `forms` plus the definitions of\n   the guest library they need, compiled unmodified under `unit-opts`\n   and published to the runtime global namespace by\n   `publish-to-globals` — so the helper's export projection can read\n   each top-level definition. The two-argument form also takes the\n   projected `exports` (names the composition already bound in the\n   runtime global namespace): their free reads publish the same way, so\n   the projection is the caller's binding for them. The program's own\n   `yang.call` call sites need no free-name declaration: the convention\n   preamble `compile-program` emits defines those names locally, and\n   the donor publication pins the `yang.call` module for the qualified\n   reads that remain.\"\n  ([forms] (lower-unit forms []))\n  ([forms exports]\n   (let [source (vec forms)\n         library (library-for source)\n         program (compile-program (concat source library) true unit-opts)\n         macros (into #{}\n                      (comp (filter #(and (seq? %) (= 'defmacro (first %))))\n                            (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second)))\n                      (concat source library))\n         names (reduce disj\n                       (into (set (top-level-names source))\n                             (concat (map (comp strip-symbol-meta second) library)\n                                     (map symbol exports)))\n                       macros)]\n     ;; `publish-to-globals` rewrites nodes after `compile-program`\n     ;; finalized them, so the unit is finalized again over its\n     ;; finished tree: the rewrite's own applications are occurrences.\n     (annotate-call-sites (u/lam [] (publish-to-globals program names #{}))))))\n\n\n(defn output\n  \"The `clj/run-main` value as test data.\"\n  [value]\n  (pr-str value))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3841,3915p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; sed -n '105,171p' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc; sed -n '120,245p' src/cljc/yang/core/prelude_admission.cljc; rg -n 'clj-prelude/|clojure\\\\.prelude|continuation-definitions|privileged.*(names|effect)|provenance.*(admi|author)' src test | head -145\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3841,3915p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; sed -n '105,171p' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc; sed -n '120,245p' src/cljc/yang/core/prelude_admission.cljc; rg -n 'clj-prelude/|clojure\\\\.prelude|continuation-definitions|privileged.*(names|effect)|provenance.*(admi|author)' src test | head -145\"","aggregated_output":"#### 8.10.7 Normal return and escaping conditions\n\nNormal return is the value of ordinary Yin application. There is no\nextra return continuation, completion packet around each result, or new\nlanguage-specific return instruction.\n\nAn escaping source exception invokes the supplied raise exit with:\n\n```clojure\n{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n :yang.call/value  original-thrown-value}\n```\n\nThis is the argument to an exceptional continuation transfer, not an\nordinary return. Returning an identical-looking map returns normal data.\nLikewise, a source program throwing a map with these keys throws that\nmap as the **payload of a new condition**; its shape is never evidence\nthat it is already a condition to forward. No engine-effect value is\nsynthesized.\n\nProtocol failures use qualified reasons such as\n`:yang.call/not-callable`, `:yang.call/invalid-invocation`, and\n`:yang.call/unsupported-binding`, with plain evidence. The caller maps\nthem to a documented local exception form retaining the complete\noriginal condition. Callee argument-binding failures retain the actual\ncallee exception under `:yang.call/thrown`. These reasons do not extend\n`dao.stream`'s outcome algebra.\n\nThe receiving caller interprets an escaping exception as follows:\n\n1. A payload valid as an exception in its own runtime retains that\n   runtime's ordinary catching and identity behavior.\n2. A runtime permitting arbitrary thrown values, such as JavaScript,\n   may deliver the original payload directly.\n3. A runtime requiring exception objects, such as Python or PHP,\n   represents an otherwise foreign payload with its own\n   `ForeignException`, retaining the complete condition and original\n   payload. Catch-all catches this local object. Typed source catches\n   match its local hierarchy, never guessed foreign class names.\n\n`ForeignException` is a proposed prelude-owned type, not a VM type.\nUnchanged rethrow propagates the original condition without adding\nwrappers. Raising a new exception creates a new condition. Crossing back\ninto a runtime recognizing the original exception restores its original\ntype and identity. Formatting a foreign payload must not implicitly\ninvoke a foreign method.\n\nThe runtime associates its generated wrapper's identity with the retained\ncondition for the wrapper's entire lifetime, separate from source-writable\nattributes. The association normally lives in private wrapper-cell\ncontents, or an equivalent task-owned identity structure with the same\nlifetime. It survives storing or returning the wrapper after the creating\ncall/catch activation has ended, and remains recoverable when that same\nwrapper is rethrown in another activation. Temporary catch state alone is\ninsufficient. Reachability/reclamation must retain the condition and its\npayload while the wrapper is live, without an ambient registry.\n\nThe runtime must not detect wrappers or unwrap arbitrary maps by their\nkey names. JavaScript may expose raw payloads for\n`:yang.call/thrown`; its local exception for a protocol failure must still\nretain that failure's qualified condition. Rethrowing the same generated\nexception forwards that complete condition, including protocol reasons;\nthrowing an unrelated value creates a new `:yang.call/thrown` condition.\nSaved activation state refers to this identity-owned association; exiting\nor restoring a catch does not destroy it.\n\nVM application/custody defects and host implementation failures remain\noperational failures. Do not catch them broadly and relabel them as\nsource exceptions. Existing explicit stream/module refusals keep their\nsource mappings under the relevant profiles.\n\n#### 8.10.8 Cleanup, re-entry, and suspension\n\nEach activation establishes its own exception bridge and saves its\ncallee runtime's dynamic context. Binding, body, and exit run under that\n(def definition-operator\n  \"The one name that is syntax rather than a name: the operator of a\n   definition `(yin/def <literal-symbol> value)`. It is legal only as the\n   operator of a two-operand application whose first operand is a literal\n   symbol other than itself. It is never a binder, a store key, a\n   definition key, a macro name, or a primitive.\"\n  'yin/def)\n\n\n(def reserved-names\n  \"The reserved set: a one-entry contract table. `require` is dynamic and\n   stays an ordinary primitive.\"\n  #{definition-operator})\n\n\n(defn reserved-name?\n  [x]\n  (contains? reserved-names x))\n\n\n(def reserved-prefix\n  \"The compiler-private name prefix (`dsg__`). Every name it begins is a\n   host or compiler temporary, never a guest name: the provenance doors\n   (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, `cell/dsg__provenance`) and the Clojure\n   frontend's own temporaries. Source admission and macro admission refuse\n   it in any executable position — a variable, a binder, or a definition\n   target. A quoted symbol carrying it stays inert data.\"\n  \"dsg__\")\n\n\n(defn reserved-prefix-name?\n  \"True when `x` is a symbol whose local name begins with `reserved-prefix`,\n   whatever its namespace: a compiler-private name no guest code may spell\n   or construct.\"\n  [x]\n  (and (symbol? x)\n       (= reserved-prefix\n          (subs (name x) 0 (min (count (name x)) (count reserved-prefix))))))\n\n\n(defn reserved-name-defect\n  \"The data of a Rule R refusal: `role` names where the reserved name\n   appeared (`:variable`, `:binder`, `:store-key`, `:definition-key`,\n   `:definition-shape`, `:primitive`, `:env`, `:store`, `:macro`,\n   `:registry`).\"\n  [role name]\n  {:rule :reserved-name, :name name, :role role})\n\n\n(defn refuse-reserved!\n  \"Throw the Rule R refusal for `name` in `role`, merged with `data`.\"\n  ([role name] (refuse-reserved! role name {}))\n  ([role name data]\n   (throw (ex-info (str \"Reserved name \" name \" used as \"\n                        (clojure.core/name role))\n                   (merge data (reserved-name-defect role name))))))\n\n\n(defn check-params!\n  \"Refuse a lambda's binders where they would bind: a reserved name\n   (Rule R), and any binder that is not a symbol, refused as\n   `:non-symbol-parameter` with the binder's coarse `:kind`. A keyword\n   parameter would otherwise write any key into a named kernel's\n   environment, `:yin.k/store-of` included. `data` is merged into the\n   refusal. Returns `params`.\"\n  ([params] (check-params! params {}))\n  ([params data]\n                                 (symbol? (first %)) (some? (second %))) components)\n                   (map? (:yang.prelude/host-modules profile))\n                   (every? (fn [[host spec]]\n                             (and (keyword? host) (map? spec)\n                                  (boolean? (:required spec))\n                                  (set/subset? (set (keys spec))\n                                               #{:required :min-bits :min-digits :min-max-items})\n                                  (every? (fn [[k v]]\n                                            (or (= k :required)\n                                                (and (integer? v) (not (neg? v))))) spec)))\n                           (:yang.prelude/host-modules profile))\n                   (or (nil? (:yang.prelude/max-effects profile))\n                       (set? (:yang.prelude/max-effects profile)))\n                   (map? store))\n      (reject-profile :schema {}))\n    (when-not (= (count components) (count (set (map first components))))\n      (reject-profile :duplicate-binding {}))\n    (loop [todo [[:enter (:yang.prelude/module profile) (:yang.prelude/root-address profile)]]\n           active #{} bindings {} manifests []]\n      (if-let [[op name addr] (peek todo)]\n        (let [todo (pop todo)]\n          (if (= op :leave)\n            (recur todo (disj active addr) bindings manifests)\n            (do\n              (when (contains? active addr)\n                (reject-profile :cycle {:address addr}))\n              (when (and (contains? bindings name) (not= (get bindings name) addr))\n                (reject-profile :duplicate-binding {:module name}))\n              (if (contains? bindings name)\n                (recur todo active bindings manifests)\n                (let [m (get store addr) tree (get store (:yin.module/tree m))]\n                  (when-not (map? m) (reject-profile :missing-manifest {:address addr}))\n                  (when-not (and (= name (:yin.module/name m))\n                                 (map? (:yin.module/requires m))\n                                 (set? (:yin.module/exports m))\n                                 (every? symbol? (:yin.module/exports m))\n                                 (every? symbol? (keys (:yin.module/requires m)))\n                                 (every? symbol? (keys (:yin.module/primitives m)))\n                                 (map? (:yin.module/primitives m))\n                                 (set? (get-in m [:yin.module/footprint :effects]))\n                                 (map? tree)\n                                 (or (not (contains? tree :root))\n                                     (= (:yin.module/tree m) (:root tree))))\n                    (reject-profile :artifact {:module name}))\n                  (when (and (= addr (:yang.prelude/root-address profile))\n                             (not= (into {} components) (:yin.module/requires m)))\n                    (reject-profile :root-pins {:module name}))\n                  ;; Ambient projection aliases require a descriptor, absent here;\n                  ;; validate-descriptor checks those collisions in P3-prime.\n                  (let [ast (if (and (:root tree) (:rows tree))\n                              (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast tree) tree)\n                        defs (module-definitions ast)]\n                    (when-not (and (= :application (:type ast))\n                                   (= (count defs) (count (set defs))))\n                      (reject-profile :export-collision {:module name})))\n                  (when (some #(string/starts-with? (clojure.core/name %) \"dsg__\")\n                              (:yin.module/exports m))\n                    (reject-profile :provenance-export {:module name}))\n                  (when (and (not= addr (get-in registry [:trusted-prelude-modules name]))\n                             (some #(contains? (:yin.module/primitives m) %)\n                                   ['cell/dsg__new-provenance 'cell/dsg__provenance]))\n                    (reject-profile :provenance-primitive {:module name}))\n                  (recur (into (conj todo [:leave name addr])\n                               (map (fn [[n a]] [:enter n a]) (:yin.module/requires m)))\n                         (conj active addr) (assoc bindings name addr) (conj manifests m)))))))\n        manifests))))\n\n\n(defn validate-profile\n  \"Validate a profile against an immutable map of verified manifests and trees.\n   Ambient projections belong to a semantics descriptor, which this API does\n   not receive; their aliases must also be checked at descriptor admission.\n   Trusted runtime identities are pinned by `:trusted-prelude-modules` in\n   the registry, as module symbol to manifest address. Returns the profile,\n   or throws a refusal before any linking or execution.\"\n  [profile artifact-store registry]\n  (let [manifests (profile-closure profile artifact-store registry)\n        effects (reduce set/union #{} (map #(get-in % [:yin.module/footprint :effects]) manifests))\n        ceiling (:yang.prelude/max-effects profile)]\n    (when (and ceiling (not (set/subset? effects ceiling)))\n      (reject-profile :effects {:effects effects :max-effects ceiling}))\n    profile))\n\n\n(defn admit-profile\n  \"Validate the closure, required host exports, and declared numeric floors.\"\n  [profile artifact-store registry host-limits]\n  (validate-profile profile artifact-store registry)\n  (let [manifests (profile-closure profile artifact-store registry)\n        hosts (:yang.prelude/host-modules profile)\n        names (into #{} (comp (mapcat #(keys (:yin.module/primitives %)))\n                              (filter #(and (namespace %) (not (vm/profile-of vm/primitives %)))))\n                    manifests)]\n    (doseq [n names]\n      (when-not (true? (get-in hosts [(keyword (namespace n)) :required]))\n        (reject-profile :host-module {:name n})))\n    (doseq [[host spec] hosts]\n      (when-not (and (map? spec) (boolean? (:required spec)))\n        (reject-profile :schema {:host host}))\n      (when (:required spec)\n        (when-not (module/module-entry (:modules registry) (symbol (name host)))\n          (reject-profile :host-module {:host host})))\n      (doseq [floor [:min-bits :min-digits :min-max-items]\n              :when (contains? spec floor)]\n        (let [minimum (get spec floor) actual (get-in host-limits [host (keyword (subs (name floor) 4))])]\n          (when-not (and (integer? minimum) (not (neg? minimum)) (number? actual) (<= minimum actual))\n            (reject-profile :host-limits {:host host :floor floor})))))\n    (admit registry names \"Prelude host export missing\" \"yang.prelude\")\n    registry))\ntest/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-dart-divergences.edn:2:{:artifact {:id :argument-vector, :tree {:root :segment/blake3-02eac587af541bc180db4109b3accd5e3981a92eb5d1d00e63d6f12d74b484b0, :rows {:segment/blake3-f3f3245cc96805674e46f83074e7ff7092aefdf6200d8b1cb1888771e524b7bd [:segment/blake3-f3f3245cc96805674e46f83074e7ff7092aefdf6200d8b1cb1888771e524b7bd :app