in/repl.cljc:322:   `call-provenance-handles`; an unclaimed admission appears in\ntest/yang/clojure/donor_link_test.clj:4:            [yang.clojure.prelude :as prelude]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:123:**Provenance:** an entry may carry an optional private `:provenance` sibling beside `:value` and `:seal`, written only by the privileged mint (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, effect `:cell/new-provenance`) at allocation, never attached, replaced, or cleared afterwards. The VM treats it as opaque data — no frontend dispatch, no reason matching, no rendering — and answers it only through the authenticated private reader (`cell/dsg__provenance`, effect `:cell/provenance`), which returns nil for anything else and is never fatal. `cell/get` returns only `:value`; `cell/set!` and `heap-write` preserve `:provenance` while updating `:value`/`:seal`. The collector traces `:provenance` as data from every live entry, from pinned entries, and as an extra root at allocation, so payload cells referenced only by a retained provenance stay reachable while the wrapper is, and become collectible when the wrapper drops.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
