{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'register.*role|export.role|role.evidence|exact role|handler contract' src/cljc/yang docs/design/yang.preludes.md | head -45; sed -n '2258,2290p;1366,1403p;2128,2165p' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc; rg -n 'capture|step-result.*:effect|make-effect' src/cljc/yin/vm/{engine,semantic}.cljc | tail -55\"","aggregated_output":"docs/design/yang.preludes.md:7:**Status:** Proposed design, 2026-11-21 (r8 — r7 reconciliation: selector, entry ABI, effect unwind, role evidence, slice repair). No implementation or completed acceptance gate is claimed.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:479:4. **Address-bound export-role evidence (r8):** qualification, closure membership, and arity alone do not establish a hook's *role* — a binary `clj/prim-get` satisfies an arity check for `:op/add`. The frontend contract or the admitted profile therefore supplies per-hook **role records** (arity + role: `:cell-accessor`, `:value`, operator, projection) resolved by recorded address, and host primitive profiles are resolved by their recorded profile addresses. A same-arity wrong-role target fails closed. **Authorization key (r8):** `(module address, export symbol, exact hook or projection role)` — the broad role `operator` alone cannot authorize (two binary operators in one published module share address, arity, and role); the same key applies to executable literal targets. Gate: substituting subtraction for addition within the same module must fail.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:574:   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; **zero state cells**). Its guest **policy tags** (`:coll/unsupported-key`, `:math/*`, `:int/*`) live in the handler contract installed by the owning entry (`clj.py/run-main` at P3′, plain `yang.clojure`'s own cold-error policy at P2′) — they are NOT part of the linker-derived VM effect footprint; only the underlying **VM effects** its definitions perform are declared through the existing linker footprint mechanism (`yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\n                      (adapter-counts env sym))]\n    (compile-lambda [av-sym] (av-dispatch env sym nil arities) env tail? macro-env)))\n\n\n(defn- apply-call?\n  \"True when `operator` is the `apply` intrinsic: not bound locally and not\n   defined by the program.\"\n  [env operator]\n  (and (= 'apply operator)\n       (not (contains? (locals env) operator))\n       (not (contains? (::defined env) operator))))\n\n\n(defn- intra-unit-fn?\n  \"True when `operator` statically names a top-level `defn`/`defn-` of this\n   unit under the outcome model: unshadowed by locals and never defined by\n   `def` or `defmacro`.\"\n  [env operator]\n  (and (outcomes? env)\n       (symbol? operator)\n       (not (contains? (locals env) operator))\n       (contains? (::defined-fns env) operator)))\n\n\n(defn- cell-ref-shaped-node\n  \"The UAST pre-filter for WHEN to ask the heap about a callee: the\n   callee could be a cell reference the VM issued — `:type :cell-ref`\n   with the `:id` and `:seal` every issued reference carries, no other\n   entries, a seal of the issued form (a 64-character string). The\n   shape never decides meaning (ruling of record, rule 2): a map\n   passing it is only worth asking about, and the `cell/authentic?`\n   query emitted beside it answers. Any `:id` spelling may name a\n   cell, so the r4 heap-id-language discriminator is retired — the\n   minted `:cell-N` restriction was itself a value-shape guess the\n   issuer never certified. A map that fails this pre-filter is never\n   asked and never dereferenced: it routes to ordinary map\n   invocation, which grants no cell capability.\"\n  [callee]\n   (if *call-site-finalizing*\n     (compile-form-1 form tail? env macro-env)\n     (binding [*call-site-finalizing* true]\n       (annotate-call-sites (compile-form-1 form tail? env macro-env))))))\n\n\n(defn- top-level-defined-fns\n  \"Plain symbols in `forms` whose top-level definitions are exclusively native\n   `defn` or `defn-` descriptors. Any `def`, `defmacro`, or external macro\n   excludes the symbol (or the unit, when macros are active) from static\n   intra-unit dispatch so dynamic admission still governs.\"\n  [forms external-macros]\n  (if (or (seq external-macros)\n          (some #(and (seq? %) (= 'defmacro (first %))) forms))\n    #{}\n    (:fns\n      (reduce (fn [{:keys [fns non-fns] :as acc} f]\n                (if-not (and (seq? f) (symbol? (second f)))\n                  acc\n                  (let [head (first f)\n                        sym  (strip-symbol-meta (second f))]\n                    (cond\n                      (= 'def head)\n                      {:fns (disj fns sym), :non-fns (conj non-fns sym)}\n\n                      (contains? #{'defn 'defn-} head)\n                      {:fns     (if (contains? non-fns sym) fns (conj fns sym))\n                       :non-fns non-fns}\n\n                      :else acc))))\n              {:fns #{}, :non-fns #{}}\n              forms))))\n\n\n(defn- program-env\n  \"The compile-time env of one program. Without `opts` it is empty: the\n   native path. `{:convention :arg-vector, :native #{symbol}, :macros\n   #{symbol}}` opts into the argument-vector convention: `:native` names the\n                (u/let1 'dsg__p (u/app (u/v 'cell/dsg__provenance) (u/v 'dsg__e))\n                        (outcome-node error-tag\n                                      (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal) (u/v 'dsg__p) (u/lit nil))\n                                                 (u/v 'dsg__e) (u/v 'dsg__p)))))))\n\n\n(defn compile-program\n  \"Compile a sequence of Clojure forms into a single Universal AST.\n   Top-level defs compile to explicit yin/def store writes, sequenced via lambda.\n   Top-level defmacros are lowered to ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...)) syntax\n   with :macro? true on the lambda; the encoder turns that flag into a\n   declaration row and the expander, not this compiler, recognizes calls.\n   The three-argument form takes `opts` opting into the argument-vector\n   convention (see `program-env`); without it the output is the native one.\"\n  ([forms] (compile-program forms true))\n  ([forms tail?] (compile-program forms tail? nil))\n  ([forms tail? opts]\n   (run! check-program-symbols! forms)\n   (let [env (program-env forms opts)]\n     ;; A discarded definition must not become a lexical binding in the\n     ;; following definitions. Descriptor entry and body closures both capture\n     ;; their environment: retaining the previous descriptor here doubles its\n     ;; paths at each definition during machine-data validation and UCF lift.\n     (letfn [(discard-result\n               [ast]\n               (if (outcomes? env) (u/then ast (u/lit nil)) ast))\n             (go\n               [forms macro-env]\n               (if (empty? forms)\n                 (compile-literal nil tail?)\n                 (let [head       (cond->> (first forms)\n                                    (outcomes? env) (lower-top-form env macro-env))\n                       rest-forms (rest forms)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:230:                             :stream-make (module/make-effect :stream/make {:capacity (nth inst 2)})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:231:                             :stream-cursor (module/make-effect :stream/cursor {:stream (get W (nth inst 2))})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:232:                             :stream-close (module/make-effect :stream/close {:stream (get W (nth inst 2))})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:233:                             :stream-put (module/make-effect :stream/put {:stream (get W (nth inst 2)) :val (get W (nth inst 3))})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:234:                             :stream-next (module/make-effect :stream/next {:cursor (get W (nth inst 2))}))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:105:  \"The one value a captured continuation is applied to. Applying a\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:107:   the argument becomes the value of the capture point. Every VM refuses\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:173:;; it in the lexical environment under the same key, so a closure captures\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2497:;; so hashing one recurses through its whole payload — the captured\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2698:   `effect` must be a `yin.vm.effect` value minted by `module/make-effect`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
