n  plain text without caller-side case folding or normalization.\n  Duplicate names remain visible until the callee's binder decides them.\n- `:yang.call/raise`: this activation's caller-supplied, non-returning\n  guest exit, accepting the condition in section 8.10.7. It closes over\n  the caller's continuation and exception machinery, never a host\n  callback or hidden global handler slot.\n\nAn absent receiver differs from one whose value is `nil`, `:py/None`,\n(def ^:private exports\n  \"`[name arities kernel]` of every export. Each kernel takes the\n   composition's limits first.\"\n  [['integer? [1] int-integer?]\n   ['normalize [1] int-normalize]\n   ['add [2] int-add]\n   ['sub [2] int-sub]\n   ['neg [1] int-neg]\n   ['mul [2] int-mul]\n   ['compare [2] int-compare]\n   ['quot-rem [2] int-quot-rem]\n   ['floor-div-mod [2] int-floor-div-mod]\n   ['pow [2] int-pow]\n   ['bit-and [2] int-bit-and]\n   ['bit-or [2] int-bit-or]\n   ['bit-xor [2] int-bit-xor]\n   ['bit-not [1] int-bit-not]\n   ['shift-left [2] int-shift-left]\n   ['shift-right [2] int-shift-right]\n   ['bit-length [1] int-bit-length]\n   ['parse [1 2] int-parse]\n   ['format [1 2] int-format]\n   ['to-float [1] int-to-float]\n   ['to-float-boxed [1] int-to-float-boxed]\n   ['true-div-boxed [2] int-true-div-boxed]\n   ['from-float-boxed [1] int-from-float-boxed]\n486:(defn- data-content=\n495:        (cbor/content= a b))))\n538:(defn- admit-key? [x]\n546:    (vector? x) (every? admit-key? x)\n547:    (map? x) (every? (fn [[k v]] (and (admit-key? k) (admit-key? v))) x)\n548:    (set? x) (every? admit-key? x)\n555:  (when-not (admit-key? x)\n610:   ['content= [2] data-content=]\n613:   ['admit-key? [1] admit-key?]\n1:;; The jolt host lane's toolchain declaration (owner fork pin, 2026-10-22)\n2:;; (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §6.1, §6.4).\n4:;; `bb bootstrap:jolt` materializes exactly this into build/tools/jolt and\n6:;; (`qualify:jolt-upgrade`, §6.4), with the explicit exception recorded below.\n7:{:jolt\n8: {:origin \"https://github.com/sonwh98/jolt\"\n11:  ;; owner decision 2026-10-22, pinned ahead of the first qualify:jolt-upgrade\n18:  :dir \"build/tools/jolt\"\n28:  ;; The fork pin carries the Sorted fix: sonwh98/jolt#2, source 7b7100c1\n30:  ;; Re-pinned 2026-10-24 (owner ruling: the JVM is canonical, jolt-lang is\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
