{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' test/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_harness.cljc; sed -n '880,955p;1190,1215p;1327,1340p' test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc; sed -n '1,145p' test/yang/cc4_corpus.clj; sed -n '145,213p' test/yang/call/conformance.clj\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness\n  \"The linked profile's composition for the JavaScript tests (T1 step S5,\n   docs/design/yang.typescript.md section 13): the namespace that requires\n   this is the publisher of `js` and `jssp`, so it publishes each module\n   once per process into one in-memory content store and serves them to\n   every linked run over a `yin.vm.linker.interpreter` composition under\n   `:trusted` derivation (the remediation ruling's R6). The `:verifying`\n   evidence is `publish-module!`'s own `link-local` links, which\n   `linked-prelude-test` asserts.\n\n   A linked run builds the program's task on one of the three vector VMs\n   with a link pair, then runs the VM and serves the pair alternately\n   until the VM stops blocking, as the REPL's drive does. The AST walker\n   is not a backend here: its link of `js` is refused `:undeclared-free`\n   until L-b.\"\n  (:require [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yang.typescript.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n            [yang.typescript.antlr.safepoint :as safepoint]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n            [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(def integer-limits\n  \"The ordinary JavaScript composition's `integer` limits.\"\n  {::integer/max-bits 100000, ::integer/max-digits 4300})\n\n\n(defn registry\n  \"The full host registry a linked JavaScript composition registers: the\n   `require` handler, then `cell`, `data`, `integer` under `limits`, and\n   `stream` — the hook module `jssp` polls a signal stream, so the\n   safepointed composition needs it even though `js` does not.\"\n  ([] (registry integer-limits))\n  ([limits]\n   (-> (module/default-registry)\n       module/register-cell-module\n       (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\n       (prelude/register-integer-module limits)\n       module/register-stream-module)))\n\n\n(def published\n  \"`js` published once into its own content store:\n   `{:store s :result r :address a :call-address ca}`. `yang.call` is\n   published first so `js` pins its shared calling runtime.\"\n  (delay\n    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n          call-result (publish/publish-module! store (call/module-spec (registry)))\n          result (publish/publish-module! store\n                                          (prelude/module-spec (registry)\n                                                               (:address call-result)))]\n      {:store store,\n       :result result,\n       :address (:address result),\n       :call-address (:address call-result)})))\n\n\n(def published-jssp\n  \"`jssp` published once into `js`'s own content store, which its pinned\n   requirement already lives in: the same shape as `published`.\"\n  (delay\n    (let [{:keys [store address]} @published\n          result (publish/publish-module!\n                   store (safepoint/module-spec (registry) address))]\n      {:store store, :result result, :address (:address result)})))\n\n\n(defn source\n  \"The serving composition over the published store: `name-env` defaults\n   to `{js <address> yang.call <address>}`, derivation `:trusted`, the test\n   being the publisher. `jssp`-serving sources pass their own `name-env`.\"\n  ([] (source {'js (:address @published),\n               'yang.call (:call-address @published)}))\n  ([name-env]\n   (link/composition {:content-store (:store @published),\n                      :name-env name-env,\n                      :derivation :trusted})))\n\n\n(defn safepoint-source\n  \"The serving composition over the published modules: `jssp` requires\n   `js`, and `js` requires `yang.call`.\"\n  []\n  (source {'js (:address @published),\n           'jssp (:address @published-jssp),\n           'yang.call (:call-address @published)}))\n\n\n(defn publish-guest-module!\n  \"One guest module's `spec` (lower/module-spec's) published into `js`'s\n   own content store, where its pinned requirements already live:\n   `publish-module!`'s answer. Guest modules are tiny beside `js`, so a\n   test may publish its own; publish imports bottom-up, the `deps` map\n   naming each import's address.\"\n  [spec]\n  (publish/publish-module! (:store @published) spec))\n\n\n(def backends\n  \"Each vector backend's root task over a program AST and composition.\"\n  {:semantic (fn [ast opts]\n               (semantic/load-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                  (vm/ast->datoms ast)\n                                  vm/ast-contract)),\n   :stack (fn [ast opts]\n            (dvm/create-vm (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                           (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))),\n   :register (fn [ast opts]\n               (rvm/create-vm (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n                              (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract)))})\n\n\n(def continues\n  \"Each vector backend's admission of the next top-level unit to a halted\n   task, as `yin.repl` admits an input line: the task keeps its store,\n   heap, module registry and module stores.\"\n  {:semantic (fn [task ast]\n               (semantic/load-ast task (vm/ast->datoms ast) vm/ast-contract)),\n   :stack (fn [task ast]\n            (let [img (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                  attached (dvm/attach-image task img vm/stack-contract)]\n              (assoc attached\n                     :pc (dvm/absolute-pc attached [(dcode/image-hash img) 0])\n                     :frames [] :stack [] :continuation []\n                     :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil))),\n   :register (fn [task ast]\n               (let [img (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n                     attached (rvm/attach-image task img vm/register-contract)\n                     pc (rvm/absolute-pc attached\n                                         [(rcode/register-hash img) 0])\n                     body (some #(when (= pc (:start %)) %)\n                                (:bodies (:segment attached)))]\n                 (assoc attached\n                        :pc pc :frames [] :continuation []\n                        :registers (vec (repeat (:registers body) nil))\n                        :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil)))})\n\n\n(defn composition\n  \"A task's composition over `modules` and the link `pair`.\"\n  [modules pair]\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\n   :capability-secret tu/secret,\n   :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin))),\n   :primitives vm/primitives,\n   :modules modules,\n   :link-request (:requests pair),\n   :link-response (:responses pair)})\n\n\n(defn drive\n  \"Run `task` and serve `pair` from `src` alternately until the task\n   stops blocking, at most 40 rounds. Returns `[task pair]`.\"\n  [task pair src]\n  (loop [task (vm/run task)\n         pair pair\n         i 0]\n    (if (and (vm/blocked? task) (< i 40))\n      (let [pair (:pair (link/serve {:pair pair, :source src}))]\n        (recur (vm/run task) pair (inc i)))\n      [task pair])))\n\n\n(defn run-linked\n  \"The finished task of the linked program `ast` on `backend`. Options:\n   `:modules` (default the full registry), `:link-source` (default the\n   `:trusted` composition over `js`), and `:prep`, applied to the task\n   before it runs (a composition handing the task its streams, binding\n   `jssp`'s signal stream among them). A refused link throws as the task's\n   own error.\"\n  ([backend ast] (run-linked backend ast {}))\n  ([backend ast {:keys [modules link-source prep]}]\n   (let [pair (link/make-pair)\n         task ((get backends backend)\n               ast\n               (composition (or modules (registry)) pair))]\n     (first (drive (if prep (prep task) task)\n                   pair (or link-source (source)))))))\n\n\n(defn runners-under\n  \"Each vector VM's runner of a linked program over `modules`: the\n   program's value.\"\n  [modules]\n  (into {}\n        (map (fn [k]\n               [k (fn [ast]\n                    (vm/value (run-linked k ast {:modules modules})))]))\n        (keys backends)))\n\n\n(def runners\n  \"The linked runners under the ordinary limits.\"\n  (runners-under (registry)))\n          (is (= bad-value (:unsupported-version res)))\n          (is (nil? (:address res))))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private publish-registry\n  \"The host registry the published-module test publishes over: the\n   `cell` and `data` host modules the `clj` and `yang.call` module\n   trees read.\"\n  (-> (module/default-registry)\n      module/register-cell-module\n      (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})))\n\n\n(defn replay-artifacts\n  \"The cc4 portable replay corpus. All admission coordinates and naming inputs\n   are supplied data. Kept public so the separately declared budget runner can\n   retain exactly the artifacts whose digests the equality gate checks.\"\n  ([] (replay-artifacts true))\n  ([annotated?]\n   (let [prepare (if annotated? identity\n                     #(walk/postwalk (fn [n]\n                                       (if (map? n)\n                                         (dissoc n :yang/call-site) n)) %))\n         forms '[(defn replay\n                   [x]\n                   (let [[a b] [x 1.5]]\n                     (+ (identity ^:replay a) (identity ^:replay a) b)))\n                 (replay 2)]\n         projected (fn [id ast token]\n                     (let [ast (prepare ast)\n                           p (encoder/project\n                               (encoder/source-envelope :cc4/replay token [ast]))]\n                       {:id id :compiled ast :tree (first (:yin/batch p))\n                        :rows (:yin/frontend-metadata p)}))\n         ast (yang/compile-program forms)\n         macro-ast (yang/compile-program\n                     '[(defmacro twin\n                         [x]\n                         (yin/if (yin/literal true) x\n                                 (yin/application (yin/variable 'f) [(yin/literal 1)])))\n                       (defn f\n                         [x]\n                         x) (twin (f 1))])\n         expansion (:result (expand-like-the-repl (prepare macro-ast)))\n         store (mem/create-content-mem)\n         call-spec (update (call/module-spec publish-registry) :ast prepare)\n         call-result (publish/publish-module! store call-spec)\n         clj-spec (update (clj-prelude/module-spec publish-registry (:address call-result))\n                          :ast prepare)\n         clj-result (publish/publish-module! store clj-spec)\n         published (fn [id result spec]\n                     (let [table (publish/published-call-site-table store result)]\n                       {:id id :compiled (:ast spec)\n                        :tree (or (:tree table) (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (:ast spec)))\n                        :rows (or (:rows table) [])\n                        :addresses (assoc (dissoc (:call-sites result) :origin)\n                                          :manifest (:address result))\n                        :published-payloads\n                        (when (:call-sites result)\n                          (mapv #(jing/get store % nil)\n                                (map (:call-sites result) [:table :provenance :record])))\n                        :provenance (publish/published-instruction-provenance store result)}))]\n     [(projected :native ast \"admission-a\")\n      (projected :argument-vector (yang/compile-program forms true yang/unit-opts)\n                 \"admission-a\")\n      (projected :lower-unit (yang/lower-unit forms) \"admission-a\")\n      (projected :prelude clj-prelude/module-uast \"admission-a\")\n      {:id :macro :compiled (prepare macro-ast) :status (:status expansion)\n       :tree (macro/packet->row-set (:tree expansion))\n       :rows (:frontend-metadata expansion) :expansion-log (:log expansion)}\n      (projected :negative ast \"admission-b\")\n      (published :yang.call call-result call-spec)\n      (published :clj clj-result clj-spec)])))\n\n\n(defn- collection-constructors\n            (is (sorted-ascending? (pair-keys c)))\n            ;; the ruled named order: :yin.k/fn, :yin.vm.data/reason,\n            ;; :yin.k/argc (key roots 1e0366, 81b62c, 8930bf)\n            (is (= [:yin.k/fn :yin.vm.data/reason :yin.k/argc]\n                   (mapv (fn [i] (:value (nth (:operands c) (inc (* 2 i)))))\n                         (range 3))))))))))\n\n\n(deftest published-module-test\n  (testing \"the markers are retrievable from the published module\"\n    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n          call-result (publish/publish-module!\n                        store (call/module-spec publish-registry))\n          call-address (:address call-result)\n          clj-result (publish/publish-module!\n                       store (clj-prelude/module-spec publish-registry\n                                                      call-address))\n          clj-address (:address clj-result)]\n      (is (some? call-address))\n      (is (some? clj-address))\n      (doseq [[label result]\n              [[\"yang.call\" call-result]\n               [\"clj\" clj-result]]]\n        (testing label\n          (is (some? (get-in result [:call-sites :record]))\n              \"the publication retains its side table beside the manifest\")\n      (is (some? (:address plain)))\n      (is (not (contains? plain :call-sites)))\n      (is (nil? (publish/published-call-site-table store plain)))))\n  (testing \"the manifest excludes the side table; the record names the manifest\"\n    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n          result (publish/publish-module!\n                   store (clj-prelude/module-spec\n                           publish-registry\n                           (:address (publish/publish-module!\n                                       store\n                                       (call/module-spec publish-registry)))))\n          address (:address result)\n          manifest (jing/get store address nil)\n          record-address (get-in result [:call-sites :record])\n(ns yang.cc4-corpus\n  \"The cc4 budget common corpus: a faithful copy of the pinned cohort\n   builder test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc/replay-artifacts at\n   origin/master 2175252d (sha256 of that file at that pin is recorded in\n   the budget findings), factored with one knob: an EXCLUDED id set, so\n   members the PRE-port pin refuses (the lower-unit member: pre-port\n   check-top-level-discard! rejects a may-fail non-final form, which the\n   port-era corpus relies on) can be omitted from BOTH revisions of the\n   measurement, keeping the pre/post corpus identical. Nothing else\n   differs from the cohort definition; the equality gate itself continues\n   to use the cohort in the test namespace.\"\n  (:require [clojure.walk :as walk]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-prelude]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]))\n\n\n(def ^:private publish-registry\n  (-> (module/default-registry)\n      module/register-cell-module\n      (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})))\n\n\n(defn- expand-like-the-repl\n  [ast]\n  (let [store (macro/seed-store\n                (macro/make-ctx {:token :callsite-test/standard-forms\n                                 :source-medium :callsite-test/standard-forms})\n                [macro/stdlib-forms])\n        ctx (macro/make-ctx {:token \"callsite-test\"\n                             :source-medium :program-in\n                             :store store})]\n    {:ctx ctx\n     :result (macro/expand-batch (encoder/program-batch ast) ctx)}))\n\n\n(defn replay-corpus\n  \"The pinned eight-member corpus. `annotated?` selects the S shape\n   (annotations retained, prepare = identity) or the B shape (C1 markers\n   stripped before projection, exactly the cohort's knob); `excluded` is\n   a set of member ids to omit (recorded in the findings with the exact\n   reason).\"\n  ([] (replay-corpus true #{}))\n  ([annotated? excluded]\n   (let [prepare (if annotated? identity\n                     (fn [ast]\n                       (walk/postwalk (fn [n]\n                                        (if (map? n)\n                                          (dissoc n :yang/call-site) n))\n                                      ast)))\n         forms (quote [(defn replay\n                         [x]\n                         (let [[a b] [x 1.5]]\n                           (+ (identity ^:replay a)\n                              (identity ^:replay a) b)))\n                       (replay 2)])\n         projected (fn [id ast token]\n                     (let [ast (prepare ast)\n                           p (encoder/project\n                               (encoder/source-envelope :cc4/replay token [ast]))]\n                       {:id id :compiled ast\n                        :tree (first (:yin/batch p))\n                        :rows (:yin/frontend-metadata p)}))\n         ast (yang/compile-program forms)\n         macro-ast (yang/compile-program\n                     (quote [(defmacro twin\n                               [x]\n                               (yin/if (yin/literal true) x\n                                       (yin/application\n                                         (yin/variable (quote f))\n                                         [(yin/literal 1)])))\n                             (defn f\n                               [x]\n                               x)\n                             (twin (f 1))]))\n         expansion (:result (expand-like-the-repl (prepare macro-ast)))\n         store (mem/create-content-mem)\n         call-spec (update (call/module-spec publish-registry) :ast prepare)\n         call-result (publish/publish-module! store call-spec)\n         clj-spec (update (clj-prelude/module-spec\n                            publish-registry (:address call-result))\n                          :ast prepare)\n         clj-result (publish/publish-module! store clj-spec)\n         published (fn [id result spec]\n                     (let [table (publish/published-call-site-table store result)]\n                       {:id id :compiled (:ast spec)\n                        :tree (or (:tree table)\n                                  (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (:ast spec)))\n                        :rows (or (:rows table) [])\n                        :addresses (assoc (dissoc (:call-sites result) :origin)\n                                          :manifest (:address result))\n                        :published-payloads\n                        (when (:call-sites result)\n                          (mapv #(jing/get store % nil)\n                                (map (:call-sites result)\n                                     [:table :provenance :record])))\n                        :provenance (publish/published-instruction-provenance\n                                      store result)}))\n         members (cond-> []\n                   (not (contains? excluded :native))\n                   (conj (projected :native ast \"admission-a\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :argument-vector))\n                   (conj (projected :argument-vector\n                                    (yang/compile-program forms true yang/unit-opts)\n                                    \"admission-a\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :lower-unit))\n                   (conj (projected :lower-unit (yang/lower-unit forms)\n                                    \"admission-a\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :prelude))\n                   (conj (projected :prelude clj-prelude/module-uast\n                                    \"admission-a\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :macro))\n                   (conj {:id :macro :compiled (prepare macro-ast)\n                          :status (:status expansion)\n                          :tree (macro/packet->row-set (:tree expansion))\n                          :rows (:frontend-metadata expansion)\n                          :expansion-log (:log expansion)})\n                   (not (contains? excluded :negative))\n                   (conj (projected :negative ast \"admission-b\"))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :yang.call))\n                   (conj (published :yang.call call-result call-spec))\n                   (not (contains? excluded :clj))\n                   (conj (published :clj clj-result clj-spec)))]\n     members)))\n    :read-export (fn [export]\n                   (list 'php/resolve-fn (str/lower-case export) export)),\n    :project (fn [name value]\n               (list 'php/declare-function! (str/lower-case name) value)),\n    :render php-h/render},\n   :python\n   {:runtime 'py,\n    :address #(:address @published-py),\n    :refusal [:yang.python.antlr/refusal :yang.python.antlr/undeclared-free],\n    :parse #(parse-ok py-parser/parse-source %),\n    :unit python-unit,\n    :run-main 'py/run-main,\n    :read-export (fn [export]\n                   (list 'py/global-get\n                         (list 'py/module-dict\n                               (list 'py/modules-ref {:py/str \"__main__\"}))\n                         {:py/str export})),\n    :project (fn [name value]\n               (list 'yin/def (list 'quote (python-export-symbol name)) value)),\n    :render py-render/output},\n   :clojure\n   {:runtime 'clj,\n    :address #(:address @published-clj),\n    :refusal [:yang.clojure/refusal :yang.clojure/undeclared-free],\n    :deps (fn [] {'yang.call (:call-address @h/published)}),\n    :parse clj-comp/read-forms,\n    :unit (fn [packet exports] (clj-comp/lower-unit packet exports)),\n    :run-main 'clj/run-main,\n    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'clj/global-get export)),\n    :project (fn [name value]\n               ;; The runtime global namespace is the one binding (as\n               ;; `js/define-global!` is for a JS caller): `lower-unit`\n               ;; reads each projected name through `clj/global-get`, so\n               ;; no task-store binding duplicates it. A caller top-level\n               ;; definition of the same name publishes after the\n               ;; projection and shadows it.\n               (list 'clj/define-global! name value)),\n    :render clj-comp/output}})\n\n\n(defn- profile\n  [frontend]\n  (or (get frontends frontend)\n      (throw (ex-info \"frontend not admitted\" {:frontend frontend}))))\n\n\n(defn- modules\n  \"The host registry, admitted by every runtime profile that checks it,\n   with the clojure guest library's host surface installed beside them.\n   Donor publication declares free names over this same registry, so a\n   clojure donor using the guest library (its `kind` and `portable`\n   hosts) publishes like it runs.\"\n  []\n  (clj-prelude/admit (php-prelude/admit (h/registry))))\n\n\n(defn- claims-call-sites?\n  \"True when map AST `ast` carries the C1 call-site key anywhere.\"\n  [ast]\n  (boolean (some #(= :yang/call-site %) (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n\n\n(defn publish-donor!\n  \"Publish the donor `source` of `frontend` as the module `module` (default\n   `xlang.donor.<frontend>`), exporting `body`, its unmodified lowered unit.\n   Answers `{:frontend :module :address :links}`.\"\n  ([frontend source]\n   (publish-donor! frontend source (symbol (str \"xlang.donor.\" (name frontend)))))\n  ([frontend source module]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
