{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '75,102p' deps.edn; sed -n '155,176p' bb.edn; sed -n '275,309p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md; rg -n 'only|:cljd|--ns' src/dev/cljd_agg.clj | head -55; rg -n 'js.*test|npm' package.json; rg -n 'defn.*carry-custody|carry-custody' src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc | head\"","aggregated_output":"           ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\n           :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\n                                      {:git/url \"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\"\n                                       :sha \"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\"}\n                                      }}\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}}\n                    :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]\n                    :main-opts [\"-m\" \"world.server\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.shell.main\"]}\n           ;; jolt host configuration (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\n           ;; §4.2-4.3), run through build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt.\n           ;; src/jolt precedes src/cljc so a host override wins; src/clj is\n           ;; listed for audited portable namespaces only (its JVM namespaces\n           ;; are selected away by :jolt reader branches, never loaded). No\n           ;; generated Java parser classes, no JS/Dart roots, and no\n           ;; dependency coordinate is fetched until a jolt-loaded namespace\n           ;; needs one.\n           :jolt {:replace-paths [\"src/jolt\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/clj\"]\n                  :replace-deps {}}\n           :jolt-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.shell.main\"]}\n           ;; composed after :jolt (-M:jolt:jolt-test): the oracle tests and\n           ;; src/dev (src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj and its sentinel)\n           :jolt-test {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]}\n           ;; DIAGNOSTIC only (-M:jolt:jolt-diag:jolt-test): a jolt stand-in\n           ;; for the corpus loader dao.jing.cbor-fixtures, whose root must\n   :task (System/exit (:exit (shell {:continue true :shutdown nil}\n                                    \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_shell_session.clj\" \"--demo\")))}\n\n  test:jolt-shell\n  {:doc \"J3: one deadline-bounded transcript corpus on JVM and jolt, held stdin, exact output/exit checks and startup timings\"\n   :task (System/exit (:exit (apply shell {:continue true :shutdown nil}\n                                    \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_shell_session.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\n\n  test:jolt-core\n  {:doc \"J2: every applicable pure suite (test/dao/host, jing, data, space, portable stream, yin/vm) under jolt, one namespace per process through src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj, fast and ^:slow alike (Q3), nonzero exit on any failure; excluded suites are printed and recorded with reason/capability/owner\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\" \"core\" *command-line-args*)))}\n\n  test:jolt-core:diag\n  {:doc \"J2 DIAGNOSTIC: test:jolt-core with the :jolt-diag alias added (the J1 corpus-loader stand-in for dao.jing.cbor-fixtures)\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\" \"core\" \"--diag\" *command-line-args*)))}\n\n  test:jolt-j2-jvm\n  {:doc \"J2: the JVM counts baseline — the same included namespaces on the JVM, one process, clojure.test run-tests per namespace (src/dev/jolt_j2_jvm_runner.clj), per-namespace counts to build/j2-logs/jvm-summary.edn for the jolt-vs-JVM diff\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\" \"jvm\" *command-line-args*)))}\n1. **G0 Iterate**: Run only the subsystem's JVM lane (`bb test:sub:clj <own>` or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`).\n   **Failure-reproduction rule (owner ruling 2026-11-01): when a test fails anywhere — a\n   gate, the nightly, or a delegate report — reproduce and fix it by running ONLY the\n   failing test, never the whole suite.** JVM: `clojure -M:test -n <ns>` (a single\n   deftest: add `-v <ns>/<var-name>`). Node: `node target/node-tests.js --test=<ns>`\n   (built by `bb build:yin-repl-node` first only if that test needs the Node REPL).\n   Dart: `bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only <ns>[/<test-name>]` (owner ruling\n   2026-11-07: the focus rule runs the failing TEST, not the namespace —\n   `NS/test-name` entries become flutter `--plain-name` filters so only the\n   named deftests execute; fall back to bare `<ns>` only when the failing\n   var inside the namespace is not yet known, and narrow as soon as it is).\n   Fix against the failing test alone, re-run it green, then climb back up\n   (G1 for the home subsystem, G2 for dependents).\n   Dart bug-chases may set `DATOM_FAIL_FAST=1` (owner ruling 2026-11-07): the\n   scoped run stops at the first failure so the report arrives in minutes instead\n   of after the full scoped set. Gate runs never set it — the merge bar needs the\n   complete pass/fail picture. All dart runs use `--reporter expanded`, which\n   streams failure names and positions inline so an interrupted run still retains\n   them (the nightly's compact reporter lost 7 failure names to its 30000s wall,\n   2026-11-06).\n   Merge bar for a fix branch (owner ruling 2026-11-07, sharpening the 2026-11-01\n   ruling): when the work is fixing already-failing tests, the previously-failing\n   tests re-run green IS the merge bar — a fix branch merges on that alone; the\n   G1/G2 climb applies to new feature slices, not to fixes. The full suite still\n   gets its end-to-end confirmation from the daily nightly (04:00 VN), which is\n   what catches collateral damage, not a pre-merge suite run.\n   Never reproduce or chase a failure with the full suite or the slow tier — the full\n   suite is not a debugging tool, and running it locally for one failing test is the\n   exact misuse that drove a laptop load average over 100 (2026-11-01). A failure that\n   only reproduces under the full suite's concurrency is diagnosed with the suite's own\n   logs (its per-shard/per-test output), not by re-running the suite repeatedly.\n2. **G1 Checkpoint**: Run the three-lane subsystem test (`bb test:sub <own>`). Proves the home suite across all three hosts before reporting ready.\n3. **G2 Land**: Run `bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes (plus `bb test:sub <own> --slow` if slow tests are present). Covers dependents across the change (for foundation subsystems like `dao.stream` or `dao.jing`, this correctly runs nearly the full suite).\n4. **G3 Master (merged in place by the 2026-11-01 owner ruling)**: The landing gate\n   for a change is the **tests that cover the feature being built** — `bb test:changed`\n7:   each `main`, and runs `flutter test` on the shards only. Shards live under\n11:     bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj [--slow-only | --slow-regex | --only NS,NS...]\n12:   --slow-only restricts the run to the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard.\n14:   --only compiles and runs only the given test namespaces (bb test:changed,\n16:   JVM-only namespace: one whose every deftest sits behind a reader\n83:(defn jvm-only?\n85:   it has no ClojureDart tests (a JVM-only namespace), as opposed to not\n101:  (let [exit (apply run!* \"clojure\" \"-M:clojuredart:cljd\" \"compile\"\n174:  (let [slow-only? (some #{\"--slow-only\"} args)\n181:        ;; runs the failing TEST, not the namespace): --only accepts NS or\n183:        ;; filters so only the named deftests execute.\n184:        {only :namespaces, test-names :tests}\n185:        (when (some #{\"--only\"} args)\n186:          (let [v (second (drop-while #(not= \"--only\" %) args))\n192:        wanted     (cond only only\n193:                         slow-only? (slow-namespaces)\n199:      (compile-tests (or only (test-namespaces))))\n203:        (let [jvm-only (if (and only (not slow-only?))\n204:                         (filter jvm-only? missing)\n206:              fatal (remove (set jvm-only) missing)]\n207:          (when (seq jvm-only)\n208:            (println \"JVM-only namespaces (compiled, no Dart tests; skipped):\"\n209:                     (str/join \", \" jvm-only)))\n212:            (when (or slow-only? only)\n97:(defn- carry-custody\n115:    (carry-custody\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
