{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_161","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented P1′ in `/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime` on `feat/p1prime-yrt-effect`, based on `f23728d3`. The patch is uncommitted, and all four new files are marked with `git add -N`.\n\n### Acceptance gates\n\n| Gate | Exact command | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Abortive and resumable effects, exactly-once cleanup, integer policy traps, shadowed `get`, depth/live-base restoration, task isolation, and forged provenance calls across semantic, stack, and register VMs | `clj -M:test -n yang.rt.effect-test -n yang.clojure.donor-link-test` | **Pass**, 9 tests, 77 assertions |\n| Clojure replay and publication goldens on JVM | `clj -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | **Pass**, 46 tests, 605 assertions |\n| Bundled/linked runtime parity and replay goldens on Node | `node target/node-tests.js --test=yang.rt.effect-test --test=yang.clojure-callsite-test` | **Pass**, 49 tests, 585 assertions |\n| Bundled/linked runtime parity on Dart | `bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yang.rt.effect-test` | **Pass**, 8 tests |\n| Bundled/linked runtime parity on Jolt | `source build/tools/jolt-env.sh` followed by `\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj yang.rt.effect-test` | **Pass**, 8 tests, 69 assertions |\n| Dependency analysis | `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` | **Pass**, zero self-loops, cycles, or multi-node SCCs. The high-degree warning list matched HEAD. |\n| Python, TypeScript, and PHP prelude and golden integrity | `git status --short --branch` and the `git diff` check below | **Pass**, byte-identical |\n\nThe four runtime host lanes ran successfully. H7 assigns native collection invocation to P2′ and the real cross-syntax unwind to P3′.\n\nAdditional focused JVM checks passed for the callable ABI and tail depth, the affected LaTTe fixtures, and the VM’s existing provenance behavior. The final Node build used a per-build test filter. An earlier Shadow CLJS invocation started broader autorun, which I stopped before restarting with that filter.\n\n```sh\nexport MISE_TRUSTED_CONFIG_PATHS=\"$PWD\"\neval \"$(mise env)\"\n\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test --config-merge \\\n  '{:ns-regexp \"^yang[.]rt[.]effect-test$|^yang[.]clojure-callsite-test$\" :autorun false}'\n\nclj -M:test -n yang.clojure-test -n yin.vm.provenance-test \\\n  -v yang.clojure-test/test-common-call-descriptor-publication \\\n  -v yang.clojure-test/test-common-call-source-admission \\\n  -v yang.clojure-test/test-common-call-non-record-refuses \\\n  -v yang.clojure-test/test-common-call-shadowed-helpers \\\n  -v yang.clojure-test/test-common-call-invalid-continuation-refuses \\\n  -v yang.clojure-test/test-common-call-rejects-named-arguments \\\n  -v yang.clojure-test/test-outcome-common-call-depth \\\n  -v yang.clojure-test/test-portable-try-outcomes\n\nclj -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test \\\n  -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-oracle-slice8-context-reconstruction \\\n  -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-oracle-site-c1-binding \\\n  -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-stamp-correspondence-nested\n\nclj -M:test -n yin.vm.provenance-test\n\ngit diff --check\ngit diff --exit-code HEAD -- \\\n  src/cljc/yang/python src/cljc/yang/typescript src/cljc/yang/php \\\n  test/yang/python test/yang/typescript test/yang/php \\\n  test/resources/yang/python test/resources/yang/typescript test/resources/yang/php\n```\n\n### Design decisions\n\n- **§4.3, “only when the handler aborts without resuming.”** The handler runs outside the matched delimiter with a temporary cleanup frame. That frame runs suspended finalizers on return or raise. A successful resumption reinstates the suspended context. A value abort supplies `nil` to cleanup.\n- **§4.4, “generic radix digit scanners.”** `scan-digits` returns the accumulated valid prefix and propagates `:bit-limit`. `all-digits?` checks the entire requested slice. The callback variant receives the original refusal keyword.\n- **§7.4, “allocates `owner` first” and “returns the value verbatim.”** An altered reference can authenticate while its invocation fails the exact owner check. Tail-position calls use a private `call-ec` transfer to release the current entry before the successor enters its own four-step boundary. Calls protected by source `try` retain their handler scope. The LaTTe fixture now verifies the existing transport refusal for live, task-owned callable cells.\n\n### Files\n\n- **Added** [effect.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yang/rt/effect.cljc), [int.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yang/rt/int.cljc), [provenance_scope.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yin/vm/provenance_scope.cljc), and [effect_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/test/yang/rt/effect_test.cljc).\n- **Updated Clojure lowering and prelude** [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc) and [prelude.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc).\n- **Updated VM provenance dispatch** [engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc), [ast_walker.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc), [semantic.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc), [stack.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc), and [register.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc).\n- **Updated fixtures and goldens** [conformance.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/test/yang/call/conformance.clj), [cc4_corpus.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/test/yang/cc4_corpus.clj), [donor_link_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/test/yang/clojure/donor_link_test.clj), [clojure_callsite_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc), [clojure_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/test/yang/clojure_test.clj), and [latte_oracle_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p1prime/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj)."}}
